    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the primary statement line 'Total revenues and other income' is composed of three sub-items: Sales and other operating revenue, Income from equity affiliates, and Other income. These are listed individually as per the schema requirement.\n2. For total_operating_cost, all items under 'Costs and other deductions' are included except for 'Interest expense', which is mapped to its own field. This follows standard practice for an integrated oil & gas company's operating costs, which include cost of goods sold (crude oil purchases), production, SG&A, depreciation, exploration, pension costs, and other operating taxes/duties.\n3. 'Other taxes and duties' is included in total_operating_cost as it is an operating expense related to production, manufacturing, and sales activities (e.g., property, excise, severance taxes), not an income tax on profit.\n4. 'Interest expense' is mapped directly to interest_expenses.\n5. 'Income tax expense' is mapped directly to taxes.\n6. 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' is mapped to net_income.\n7. The supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of Other income, Depreciation, Other taxes, Income taxes) but do not change the top-level mapping from the primary statement. They are used for context but not for extraction as they are sub-components already summed in the primary statement lines.\n8. Numbers are extracted as presented in the statement (millions of dollars). Parentheses indicate negative values, but all values mapped here are positive in the source as they are presented as absolute expenses that reduce income.\n9. Scale is 1,000,000 (millions).",
